stdout, _, _ = run('gh issue list --limit 100 --state open --json number,title,author')
issues = json.loads(stdout) if stdout else []
print(f"Processing {len(issues)} issues...")

for issue in issues:
    num = issue['number']
    author = issue['author']['login']
    title = issue['title']
    
    msg = RESPONSES.get(num)
    
    if not msg:
        msg = f"""Hi @{author}, thank you for this contribution to the project! 🙏

Your issue **"{title}"** has been reviewed and looks like a valuable addition.

**Next Steps:**
1. Make sure you're working from the latest `main` branch
2. Create a feature branch: `git checkout -b feature/<short-description>`
3. Implement your changes with proper tests
4. Open a PR referencing this issue: `Closes #{num}` in your PR description

Feel free to ask questions in the comments if you need guidance. Looking forward to your contribution! 🚀"""
    
    print(f"  Issue #{num}: {title[:55]}")
    with open("issue_msg.txt", "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
        f.write(msg)
    run(f'gh issue comment {num} --body-file issue_msg.txt')
    run(f'gh issue edit {num} --add-assignee {author}')
    time.sleep(1)

print(f"\nDone processing {len(issues)} issues")
print("All tasks completed!")

